@meta
id: 06-01
title: All the way back with zero
chapter: 06
type: lesson
skills: line-start
par: 20
minutes: 3
vscode: Home, or clicking in the gap before the first character
open: constants.ts

@brief
One line, eighty characters wide, and two things wrong with it. The
declaration is never terminated, and it is not exported, so nothing else in
the service can see these values.

Terminate the line and export the declaration. Leave everything between the
two ends exactly as it is.

The second half of the job starts at the far left of the line. You have just
been at the far right. Getting between the two is what this chapter is about,
and the first key does it in one press regardless of how long the line is.

@keys
| `0` | the first column of the line, blank or not |
| `A` | append at the end of the line |
| `i` | insert to the left of the cursor |

@hints
Do the end of the line first, while you are already there. Then you need to
travel the whole width of the line leftwards.
--
`0` — the digit zero, not the letter O — puts the cursor in column one. It
takes one press whether the line is ten characters or two hundred.
--
`A` `;` `Esc` closes the statement. Then `0`, then `i`, then type the keyword
and a space, then `Esc` and save.

@solution
    A ; <Esc> 0 i export  <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Seventeen keystrokes, seven of them the word `export`.

`0` is the bluntest motion in vim and one of the most used. It ignores
indentation, ignores words, ignores everything: column one, now. The cost of
using it does not grow with the line, which is the whole point. Holding `h`
across eighty characters takes eighty presses and your full attention;
`b` counts words and stops in the wrong places around punctuation like
`=` and `,`.

Two habits worth forming here. Repair the end of a line while you are at the
end of it, rather than travelling back and forth. And when you are lost in
the middle of a long line, `0` is a reset button — it costs one key and puts
you somewhere you understand.

@start constants.ts
const REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS = 30, MAX_PARTIAL_REFUNDS = 3, RETRY_BACKOFF_MS = 250

@expected constants.ts
export const REFUND_WINDOW_DAYS = 30, MAX_PARTIAL_REFUNDS = 3, RETRY_BACKOFF_MS = 250;
